# Thesis-grade commit history

This monorepo is a *praca inżynierska*. Dense `git log` is a primary source for hardware/firmware chronology chapters. Sparse or squash-style history is a liability for the paper.

**This project rule overrides any global “only commit when the user asks” habit.** Create commits as work lands. Honor an explicit user “don’t commit yet.”

## Cadence (bias: more commits)

Commit after each coherent unit — not at end of session:

1. One concern finished (driver stub, net fix, LaTeX subsection, OpenSpec artifact set)
2. Build/flash milestone reached (or intentional failing checkpoint is describable)
3. Architecture/decision change locked in docs
4. Before switching tasks or ending a turn that changed tracked files

**Do not** wait for the whole feature/chapter. **Do not** one catch-all commit for mixed PCB + firmware + docs.

Split: app → flash/tooling → docs. Prefixes: `thesis:`, `hardware:`, `firmware:`, `web:`.

If unsure: **commit**.

## Message depth (thesis-readable)

Subject: imperative, why-focused, ~50–72 chars, with prefix.

Body: write for future-you drafting the thesis — not a file list. Include when relevant:

- **Why** this change (constraint, measurement, promotor/APD scope, power, pin rule)
- **What was tried / discarded** (so chronology chapters can say “we rejected X because…”)
- **Decision locked** (component, pin, stack choice) and what it replaces if anything
- **How to verify** (build target, flash, expected LED/UART behavior) when non-obvious

```text
# ❌ BAD
WIP
fix stuff
Update firmware files

# ✅ GOOD
firmware: wake on LIS3DH INT1 for alarm dismiss

Motion dismiss must interrupt deep sleep without polling.
INT1 on high-G / activity threshold; INT2 reserved for
free-fall experiments. Verified: DK LED toggle on INT1
while main loop stays in WFE.
```

## Safety (unchanged)

- No force-push, no config edits, no secrets / KiCad junk / LaTeX build outputs
- Stage only related files (no blanket `git add .` with mixed concerns)
- HEREDOC for message; amend only if user asks and amend-safety holds
